    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the \"manageable challenge\" angle, but I'm worried about the wording. If we call them \"mitigation strategies,\" it implies there is an actual risk present. Wouldn't it be better to just characterize the soil as \"stable with appropriate foundation support\" and leave out any mention of liquefaction or seismic concerns entirely? If we don't bring it up, they might not even ask about it.",
